{"id":"NCT07900633","title":"A Study of Eloralintide (LY3841136) in Participants With Obesity or Overweight, Type 2 Diabetes, and Increased Cardiovascular Risk","official":"A Phase 3, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Once-Weekly Eloralintide in Adult Participants With Obesity or Overweight, Type 2 Diabetes, and Increased CV Risk","summary":"The main purpose of this study is to evaluate the efficacy and safety of eloralintide compared with a placebo in participants with obesity or overweight, type 2 diabetes, and increased cardiovascular risk.","conditions":["Obesity","Overweight","Cardiovascular Diseases","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Eloralintide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Have type 2 diabetes\n* Have a HbA1c value between ≥ 6.5% and ≤ 9.5% at screening\n* Are on stable treatment with an unchanged dose of at least 1 and no more than 4 antihyperglycemic therapies for at least 90 days before screening\n* Have an increased risk of cardiovascular events\n* Have a BMI ≥ 25.0 kg/m2 at screening\n* Have a stable body weight (\\<5% body weight change) for 90 days prior to screening\n* Have a history of at least one self-reported unsuccessful dietary effort to reduce body weight\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Have a prior or planned surgical treatment for obesity (liposuction, cryolipolysis, or abdominoplasty allowed if performed \\>1 year before screening)\n* Have a prior or planned endoscopic procedure and/or device-based therapy for obesity (prior device-based therapy acceptable if device removal was more than 6 months prior to screening)\n* Have type 1 diabetes\n* Have a history or diagnosis of New York Heart Association Functional Classification IV congestive heart failure\n* Have had within 60 days prior to screening:\n\n  * acute myocardial infarction\n  * stroke\n  * hospitalization for congestive heart failure, or\n  * coronary, peripheral, or carotid artery revascularization procedure\n* Have received treatment combining sulfonylurea and insulin within 90 days prior to screening","minAge":"45 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":3000,"start":"2026-12","pcd":"2029-11","upd":"2026-11-03","sponsor":"Eli Lilly and Company","areas":["other"],"central":["Trial questions or participation questions: 1-877-CTLILLY (1-877-285-4559) or · 317-615-4559 · LillyTrials@Lilly.com","Physicians interested in becoming principal investigators please contact · clinical_inquiry_hub@lilly.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Central Research Associates","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35205","s":"NYR","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"2053271077"},{"f":"University of Alabama - Department of Nutrition Sciences","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35294","s":"NYR","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"205-996-4733"},{"f":"Nephrology Consultants","city":"Huntsville","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35805","s":"NYR","lat":34.7304,"lon":-86.5859,"c":"2565334626"},{"f":"Smiths Medical Center","city":"Apache Junction","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85120","s":"NYR","lat":33.4151,"lon":-111.5496,"c":"404-585-8358"},{"f":"Prime Medical Group, LLC dba Gilbert Center for Family Medicine, LLC","city":"Gilbert","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85296","s":"NYR","lat":33.3528,"lon":-111.789,"c":"480-691-2213"},{"f":"Elite Clinical Studies, LLC","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85018","s":"NYR","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":"602-788-3437"},{"f":"Southwest Kidney Institute - Surprise","city":"Surprise","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85374","s":"NYR","lat":33.6306,"lon":-112.3332,"c":"(480) 610-6100"},{"f":"Valley Clinical Trials, Inc.","city":"Covina","pr":"California","zip":"91723","s":"NYR","lat":34.09,"lon":-117.8903,"c":"310-309-9491"},{"f":"Neighborhood Healthcare Institute of Health","city":"Escondido","pr":"California","zip":"92025","s":"NYR","lat":33.1192,"lon":-117.0864,"c":"760